It is Saturday afternoon in May.
My shift at the café is over.
"Bye, Elif!" I say.
"See you next week, Maya!" she answers.
I ride my bicycle back to my flat.
The weather is beautiful today.
The sun is shining brightly.
It is much warmer now than in April.
My thick winter coat is already in the wardrobe.
I do not need it anymore.
But I have a small problem.
I have almost no summer clothes.
All my jumpers are too thick.
I really need a light summer jacket.
And I also want to buy a new shirt.
The afternoon is perfect for shopping.
I take my backpack and go back outside.
I am looking forward to the city.
